claim_principal: pi-agent
author: claude
estimated_minutes: 720
acceptance_criteria: "A generation with no parent is accepted as the seed generation and reports itself as such; every later generation requires a parent that exists and is either the registered seed or itself promoted, so a seed may parent a candidate without being promoted while any non-seed parent must be promoted; the collection runs named by a generation must reference the parent's policy and are refused when they do not; the recorded base checkpoint, environment version and reward-spec version identities are content-addressed so a silently swapped artifact fails to resolve; an edit to an environment or reward specification is reachable in reverse to every generation whose collection runs used it, transitively through the parent chain; the declared edge types are enumerated in the specification rather than inferred"
resolution: Added test/lineage.test.ts exercising generation registration and ancestry building.
expected_result: "A generation with no parent is the seed; a later generation requires a parent that is the seed or a promoted generation, refused as parent_not_promoted otherwise; collection runs reference the parent policy; provenance identities are content-addressed."
actual_result: "test/lineage.test.ts passes, including the registered-seed exception and the parent_not_promoted refusal for a non-seed parent; index.ts and lineage.ts at 100/100/100 lines/branches/functions."
